From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:43:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: flush consoles before emergency cold reset

Use the shared cold escape to give printk threads a bounded opportunity
to deliver evidence before IRQs and other CPUs stop. A pstore dump alone
is not recoverable evidence across an iOS boot.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/teardown.inc | 9 +++------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/teardown.inc b/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/teardown.inc
index 93eb34f79..252c3e488 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/teardown.inc
+++ b/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/teardown.inc
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+#include <linux/soc/apple/cold-reset.h>
+
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR MIT
 /*
  * Kernel glue for the GPU teardown state machine (teardown.h).
@@ -686,12 +688,7 @@ static int g5p_td_reboot_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action,
 		if (action == SYS_RESTART && ret && ret != -EALREADY) {
 			dev_emerg(g->dev,
 				  "GPU-KQ unsafe handover ret=%d; forcing cold watchdog reset to iOS\n", ret);
-			/* PANIC dump reason reaches default pstore filters without
-			 * entering panic() or consulting panic_timeout.
-			 */
-			kmsg_dump_desc(KMSG_DUMP_PANIC, "GPU-KQ cold-reset fallback (no panic)");
-			WRITE_ONCE(reboot_mode, REBOOT_COLD);
-			emergency_restart();
+			apple_cold_reset("GPU-KQ cold-reset fallback (no panic)");
 		}
 	}
 	{
